---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const baseUrl = (import.meta.env.BASE_URL || '/').replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Layout lang="en" title="Parameter Reference — OmniPrep" description="OmniPrep — unified multimodal MRI preprocessing and analysis pipeline." active="docs">

    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="breadcrumb"><a href={`${baseUrl}/`}>Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><a href={`${baseUrl}/docs/`}>Documentation</a><span class="sep">/</span>Parameter reference</div>
        <h1>Parameter Reference</h1>
        <p class="lead">The complete command-line interface of OmniPrep, organized by category. Every option is documented with its type, default value, and behavior.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="docs-layout container">
      <aside class="toc">
        <div class="toc-title">On this page</div>
        <ul>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#required">Required options</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#general-options">General options</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#atlas-options">Atlas &amp; ROI options</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#bold-options">BOLD fMRI options</a></li>
          <li><a href="#bold-basic">BOLD basics</a></li>
          <li><a href="#bold-spatial">Spaces &amp; resampling</a></li>
          <li><a href="#bold-motion">Motion &amp; scrubbing</a></li>
          <li><a href="#bold-denoise">Denoising</a></li>
          <li><a href="#bold-metrics">Metrics &amp; ROI</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#dwi-options">DWI options</a></li>
          <li><a href="#dwi-basic">DWI basics</a></li>
          <li><a href="#dwi-tensor">DTI &amp; CSD</a></li>
          <li><a href="#dwi-track">Tractography</a></li>
          <li><a href="#dwi-connectome">Connectome</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#hpc-env">HPC environment variables</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#examples">Examples</a></li>
        </ul>
      </aside>

      <article class="doc-content">

        <p class="xref"><strong>Where things fit:</strong> see how each option maps to a processing step in <a href={`${baseUrl}/docs/pipeline/`}>Processing pipeline ↗</a> · see what each option produces in <a href={`${baseUrl}/docs/outputs/`}>Outputs &amp; derivatives ↗</a> · for a running start, see <a href={`${baseUrl}/docs/quickstart/`}>Quick start ↗</a></p>

        <section id="required">
          <h2>Required options</h2>
          <div class="param" id="p-fs_license_file">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--fs-license-file <span class="arg">&lt;PATH&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-required">required</span>
              <span class="badge badge-type">string</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Path to a valid FreeSurfer license file required for FreeSurfer/FastSurfer surface reconstruction and parcellation.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Docker / single-node Singularity:</strong> provide the in-container mounted path (e.g. <code>/license.txt</code>) matching your <code>-v</code> or <code>--bind</code> mount.</li>
                <li><strong>HPC wrapper (<code>omniprep_singularity.sh</code>):</strong> provide the host absolute path; the wrapper handles bind-mounting automatically.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="general-options">
          <h2>General options</h2>

          <div class="param" id="p-work_dir">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--work-dir <span class="arg">&lt;PATH&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: output_dir/WorkDir</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Path where intermediate results of OmniPrep should be stored. If not specified, the <code>WorkDir</code> directory will be generated by default under the output path.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-tasks">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--tasks <span class="arg">anat bold dwi</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: "anat bold dwi"</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify which preprocessing workflows to run. Multiple tasks are passed as space-separated values.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>anat</code> — T1w structural MRI preprocessing</li>
                <li><code>bold</code> — BOLD fMRI preprocessing</li>
                <li><code>dwi</code> — diffusion MRI preprocessing</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-age_group">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--age-group <span class="arg">&#123;adult|pediatric|infant&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: adult</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the participant age group for age-appropriate MRI preprocessing.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>infant</code> — under 2 years</li>
                <li><code>pediatric</code> — 2 to under 18 years</li>
                <li><code>adult</code> — 18 years and older</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-participant_label">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--participant-label <span class="arg">sub-001 sub-002 ...</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-type">string</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify one or more participants to process. If this option is not provided, all participants in the <a href="https://bids.neuroimaging.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brain Imaging Data Structure (BIDS)</a> directory will be processed.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-exclude_participant_label">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--exclude-participant-label <span class="arg">sub-003 sub-004 ...</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-type">string</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify participants to exclude from processing. If specified, the designated participants will be ignored.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-session_label">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--session-label <span class="arg">ses-pre ses-post ...</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-type">string</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>A space-delimited list of session identifiers or a single identifier. If not specified, all existing sessions in the BIDS directory will be processed.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-subjects_dir">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--subjects-dir <span class="arg">&lt;PATH&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: output_dir/derivatives/omniprep/Recon</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Path to a pre-existing T1w derivatives directory.</p>
              <p>This option is required if <code>anat</code> is <em>not</em> included in <code>--tasks</code> but BOLD or DWI preprocessing is requested, because BOLD and DWI workflows depend on structural derivatives such as T1w images, masks, surfaces, segmentations, and parcellations. If no path is specified, <code>output_dir/derivatives/omniprep/Recon</code> is used by default.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-skip_bids_validation">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--skip-bids-validation</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Skip BIDS validation. By default, OmniPrep validates the input dataset as a BIDS dataset before processing. Use this option only if you are confident that the input data are organized correctly or if validation is handled externally.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-clean_workdir">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--clean-workdir</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Delete intermediate files as soon as downstream steps finish consuming them (after verifying the step output is non-empty). This substantially reduces peak disk usage for large cohorts.</p>
              <p><strong>Best practice with <code>--resume</code>:</strong></p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Production large cohorts:</strong> strongly recommended. If a run is interrupted (OOM, power loss, node restart) or you append new subjects, keep the same options and add <code>--resume</code> to resume safely.</li>
                <li><strong>Debugging:</strong> disable <code>--clean-workdir</code> while iterating on parameters. Do not toggle <code>--clean-workdir</code> mid-cohort, or cache hashes may invalidate and upstream tasks may fail to find deleted intermediates.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-device">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--device <span class="arg">&#123;auto|cpu|0|1|2|...&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: auto</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the compute device.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>auto</code> — automatically select available compute devices.</li>
                <li><code>cpu</code> — disable GPU acceleration and run GPU-capable steps on CPU where supported.</li>
                <li><code>0, 1, 2, ...</code> — run GPU-enabled steps on the specified GPU device ID.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-cpus">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--cpus <span class="arg">&#123;auto|8|16|20|...&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: auto</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Maximum number of CPU cores available to the workflow.</p>
              <p>When set to <code>auto</code>, OmniPrep automatically detects the total number of CPU cores in the runtime environment and uses that value for Nextflow. When customizing, ensure the value you set does not exceed the actual number of CPU cores.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-memory">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--memory <span class="arg">&#123;auto|16|24|32|64|...&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: auto</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Maximum memory available to the workflow, in GB.</p>
              <p>When set to <code>auto</code>, OmniPrep automatically detects the amount of memory available in the runtime environment and allocates 90% of it to Nextflow.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-nthreads">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--nthreads <span class="arg">&lt;N&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: 8</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Number of threads used by multi-threaded applications. Set to <code>0</code> to disable explicit multi-threading control. If this value is too high, efficiency will actually decrease, so <code>8</code> is recommended.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-ignore_error">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--ignore-error</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Continue the workflow when selected non-critical errors are encountered. Useful for large datasets, but use with caution — failed derivatives may be missing for some subjects.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-resume">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--resume</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Resume a previous Nextflow run. Completed tasks will be reused from the cache instead of being recomputed. Use this after an unexpected termination to avoid re-running already-completed tasks.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-no_qc">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--no-qc</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Disable generation of the quality control results, including all QC figures (SVG) and interactive HTML QC reports. Only recommended for maximum-speed or temporary workflow testing.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-debug">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--debug</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Enable debug logging, printing more detailed parameter-parsing results, configuration file paths and runtime diagnostics to help troubleshoot deployment issues.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="atlas-options">
          <h2>Atlas &amp; ROI-level derivative options</h2>
          <p class="lead-copy">OmniPrep uses a modular <strong>3-layer atlas composition</strong> (cortex + subcortex + cerebellum). The selected atlas combination is applied uniformly to T1w morphometric features, BOLD ROI time series / functional connectivity / local metrics, and DWI structural connectomes.</p>

          <div class="param" id="p-cortex_atlas">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--cortex-atlas <span class="arg">DK Glasser Schaefer200P7N Brainnetome</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: DK</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify one or more cortical atlases for ROI-level derivatives. Multiple atlases are passed as space-separated values.</p>
              <p><strong>Built-in cortical atlases:</strong></p>
              <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                  <thead><tr><th>Atlas</th><th>Parcellation</th><th>Typical use</th></tr></thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>DK</code></td><td>Desikan-Killiany anatomical atlas (68 cortical regions)</td><td>Cortical thickness/area/volume morphometry baseline, cross-age studies</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>a2009s</code></td><td>Destrieux fine sulco-gyral atlas (148 cortical regions)</td><td>High-resolution anatomical morphometry</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Glasser</code></td><td>HCP-MMP1.0 multimodal atlas (360 cortical regions)</td><td>High-precision functional connectivity &amp; structural connectomes</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Brainnetome</code></td><td>Brainnetome atlas (210 cortical regions)</td><td>Multimodal brain networks &amp; clinical neuroimaging</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Schaefer&#123;100..1000&#125;P&#123;7N,17N&#125;</code></td><td>Schaefer functional atlas (100–1000 regions, 7/17 networks, e.g. Schaefer200P7N, Schaefer400P17N)</td><td>Resting-state FC, graph theory &amp; GNN modeling</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
              <p style="margin-top:12px"><strong>Custom cortical atlases:</strong> mount surface parcellation files (<code>.annot</code> or <code>.gcs</code>) together with their original and reordered LUT files under <code>/opt/atlas</code> inside the container.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-subcortex_atlas">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--subcortex-atlas <span class="arg">&#123;none|freesurfer|auto|&lt;AtlasName&gt;&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: none</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Subcortical parcellation strategy combined with the cortical atlas(es):</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>none</code> — cortical-only parcellation; exclude subcortical regions.</li>
                <li><code>freesurfer</code> — append 21 FreeSurfer subcortical regions from the subject's <code>aseg.mgz</code> (see <code>omniprep/atlas/LUT</code> for region definitions). The robust general-purpose default; strongly recommended for infants/young children (zero template-registration error).</li>
                <li><code>auto</code> — use each cortical atlas's native subcortical parcellation if available (<code>&lt;Atlas&gt;_space-MNI152XXX_subcortex.nii.gz</code> via SynthMorph, or <code>&lt;Atlas&gt;.gca</code> via <code>mri_ca_label</code>); otherwise fall back to FreeSurfer subcortical regions.</li>
                <li><code>&lt;AtlasName&gt;</code> — apply a standalone volumetric subcortical atlas (e.g. <code>TianS1</code>, <code>TianS2</code>, <code>Brainnetome</code>) to all selected cortical atlases via SynthMorph (once per subject). Requires the NIfTI file and its LUT under <code>/opt/atlas</code>.</li>
              </ul>
              <p><strong>Built-in subcortical atlases (for <code>&lt;AtlasName&gt;</code>):</strong></p>
              <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                  <thead><tr><th>Atlas</th><th>Parcellation</th><th>Typical use</th></tr></thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>FreeSurfer</code></td><td>21 subcortical structures from <code>aseg.mgz</code></td><td>Robust general-purpose default; recommended for infants/young children</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Brainnetome</code></td><td>Brainnetome subcortical parcellation</td><td>Multimodal brain networks &amp; clinical neuroimaging</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>TianS1</code></td><td>Tian et al. subcortical atlas, scale 1 (16 regions)</td><td>Coarse subcortical functional/anatomical parcellation</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>TianS2</code></td><td>Tian et al. subcortical atlas, scale 2 (32 regions)</td><td>Balanced resolution for functional connectivity</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>TianS3</code></td><td>Tian et al. subcortical atlas, scale 3 (50 regions)</td><td>Finer subcortical parcellation</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>TianS4</code></td><td>Tian et al. subcortical atlas, scale 4 (54 regions)</td><td>Highest-resolution subcortical parcellation</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-cerebellum_atlas">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--cerebellum-atlas <span class="arg">&#123;none|&lt;AtlasName&gt;&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: none</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Cerebellar parcellation strategy registered via SynthMorph (once per subject) and appended to cortical/subcortical parcellations:</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>none</code> — exclude a dedicated cerebellar parcellation.</li>
                <li><code>&lt;AtlasName&gt;</code> — apply a volumetric cerebellar atlas (e.g. <code>SUIT</code>, <code>Buckner17</code>, <code>MDTB</code>). Requires <code>&lt;AtlasName&gt;_space-MNI152XXX_cerebellum.nii.gz</code> and its LUT under <code>/opt/atlas</code>.</li>
              </ul>
              <p><strong>Built-in cerebellar atlases (for <code>&lt;AtlasName&gt;</code>):</strong></p>
              <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                  <thead><tr><th>Atlas</th><th>Parcellation</th><th>Typical use</th></tr></thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>AAL3</code></td><td>Automated Anatomical Labeling v3 with cerebellar subdivision</td><td>Whole-brain (incl. cerebellum) anatomical labeling</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Buckner7</code></td><td>Buckner et al. functional connectivity cerebellum, 7 networks</td><td>Coarse cerebello-cortical functional parcellation</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Buckner17</code></td><td>Buckner et al. functional connectivity cerebellum, 17 networks</td><td>Fine cerebello-cortical functional parcellation</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>NettekovenSym32</code></td><td>Nettekoven symmetric cerebellar atlas (32 regions)</td><td>Bilateral/symmetric cerebellar mapping</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>SUIT</code></td><td>Spatially Unbiased Infratentorial Template (SUIT) atlas</td><td>Detailed lobular cerebellar anatomy</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
              <p><strong>Automatic de-duplication:</strong> when combined with FreeSurfer <code>aseg</code>, the coarse left/right cerebellar cortex labels (8, 47) are automatically removed and replaced by the fine cerebellar atlas labels to avoid overlapping regions.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="bold-options">
          <h2>BOLD fMRI options</h2>

          <h3 id="bold-basic">BOLD basics</h3>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_task_type">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-task-type <span class="arg">task1 task2 task3 ...</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-type">string</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify BOLD task names to process, such as <code>rest</code> or task-specific names. Multiple tasks are passed as space-separated values.</p>
              <p>Example: <code>--bold-task-type rest nback</code></p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_skip_frame">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-skip-frame <span class="arg">&lt;N&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: 0</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Number of initial BOLD volumes to remove before denoising. Commonly used to remove non-steady-state volumes affected by unstable MR signal.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_sdc">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-sdc <span class="arg">&#123;auto|true|false&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: auto</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Control susceptibility distortion correction (SDC) for BOLD fMRI:</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>auto</code> — run SDC when fieldmaps (fmap) are present; otherwise skip automatically.</li>
                <li><code>true</code> — require SDC for all subjects (errors if any subject lacks a fieldmap).</li>
                <li><code>false</code> — disable SDC for all subjects.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_cifti">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-cifti</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Generate CIFTI-format BOLD outputs. The default CIFTI output space is the HCP-style <code>91k</code> grayordinate space. Disabled by default unless this option is specified.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 id="bold-spatial">Spaces &amp; resampling</h3>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_surface_spaces">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-surface-spaces <span class="arg">&lt;SPACE&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: fsaverage6</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the surface template space for BOLD surface outputs.</p>
              <p><strong>Supported values:</strong></p>
              <div class="pill-row">
                <span class="pill hl">fsnative</span>
                <span class="pill hl">fsaverage</span>
                <span class="pill hl">fsaverage1</span>
                <span class="pill hl">fsaverage2</span>
                <span class="pill hl">fsaverage3</span>
                <span class="pill hl">fsaverage4</span>
                <span class="pill hl">fsaverage5</span>
                <span class="pill hl">fsaverage6</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_output_space">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-output-space <span class="arg">&lt;SPACE:res-N&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: MNI152NLin6Asym:res-2</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the template space and resolution for volumetric BOLD outputs. Supports optional cohort and resolution settings.</p>
              <p><strong>Registration strategy:</strong></p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Adults:</strong> direct registration from T1w to the specified output space.</li>
                <li><strong>Infants and children:</strong> an age-appropriate MNIInfant or MNIPediatric cohort is automatically selected based on <code>age_months</code>.
                  <ul>
                    <li>If the selected cohort matches the output space, register directly from T1w to that space (single-stage).</li>
                    <li>Otherwise, register from T1w to the age-matched cohort, then to the specified output space (two-stage).</li>
                  </ul>
                </li>
              </ul>
              <p>All transforms are combined to resample BOLD only once.</p>
              <p><strong>Age detection (<code>age_months</code>):</strong> automatically read age from BIDS <code>sessions.tsv</code> (preferred) or <code>participants.tsv</code>. Supported fields: <code>age_days</code> &gt; <code>age_weeks</code> &gt; <code>age_months</code> &gt; <code>age</code> (years). All ages are converted to months (<code>age_months</code>).</p>
              <p><strong>Age-specific templates:</strong></p>
              <ul>
                <li>Under 5 years — <code>MNIInfant</code> (age-matched cohort).</li>
                <li>5 to under 18 years — <code>MNIPediatricAsym</code> (age-matched cohort).</li>
                <li>18 years and older — Adult template.</li>
              </ul>
              <p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>
              <div class="pill-row">
                <span class="pill hl">MNI152NLin6Asym:res-2</span>
                <span class="pill hl">MNI152NLin2009cAsym:res-2</span>
                <span class="pill hl">MNIInfant:cohort-4:res-2</span>
                <span class="pill hl">MNIPediatricAsym:cohort-2:res-2</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 id="bold-motion">Motion &amp; scrubbing</h3>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_confounds">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-confounds</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Compute BOLD confound regressors, including motion parameters, tissue-based signals, outlier regressors, and other nuisance variables used for BOLD denoising.</p>
              <p>OmniPrep generates the <code>motion_outlier_XXX</code> parameters for motion frame detection. The Power method is used for motion frame detection by default, with a threshold of 0.2 for framewise displacement (FD).</p>
              <p>This option is automatically enabled when <a href="#p-bold_denoise"><code>--bold-denoise</code></a>, <a href="#p-bold_roi_timeseries"><code>--bold-roi-timeseries</code></a>, or <a href="#p-bold_roi_pearson_fc"><code>--bold-roi-pearson-fc</code></a> is enabled.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_scrubbing">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-scrubbing</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Once scrubbing is enabled, OmniPrep processes motion frames during the denoising step of the post-processing workflow, in accordance with the strategy defined by the <code>bold_scrubbing_strategy</code> variable. The motion frame markers are defined by the <code>motion_outlier_XXX</code> and <code>scrub_fd_XXX_0pX_mask</code> values in the confounds file.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_scrubbing_strategy">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-scrubbing-strategy <span class="arg">&#123;regression|interpolation&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: regression</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the scrubbing strategy. Currently, only the <code>regression</code> and <code>interpolation</code> methods are supported.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>regression</code> — the motion frames will be regressed out during the regression of the covariates.</li>
                <li><code>interpolation</code> — the motion frames will be processed using the PCHIP method.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_fd_type">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-fd-type <span class="arg">&#123;power|jenkinson&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: power</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the type of FD used to detect motion frames. Currently, the <code>power</code> and <code>jenkinson</code> methods are supported.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>power</code> — the FD value is stored in the <code>framewise_displacement</code> field of the confounds file.</li>
                <li><code>jenkinson</code> — the value is stored in the <code>rmsd</code> field of the confounds file.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_fd_threshold">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-fd-threshold <span class="arg">&lt;N&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: 0.2</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the threshold for FD. When this threshold is exceeded, the frame is considered to be a motion frame.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_scrubbing_prev">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-scrubbing-prev <span class="arg">&lt;N&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: 0</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Number of volumes preceding each detected motion outlier to additionally mark as outliers.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_scrubbing_later">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-scrubbing-later <span class="arg">&lt;N&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: 0</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Number of BOLD volumes following each detected motion outlier that will also be marked as outliers. A value of <code>0</code> disables forward temporal expansion.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 id="bold-denoise">Denoising</h3>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_denoise">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-denoise</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Perform BOLD denoising based on the generated confound regressors. Depending on the selected options, this may include nuisance regression, detrending, temporal filtering, and removal of initial volumes (<code>--bold-skip-frame</code>).</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_denoise_strategy">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-denoise-strategy <span class="arg">&lt;STRATEGY&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: motion24_wm_csf</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the BOLD denoising strategy.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>motion6</code> — six rigid-body motion parameters: <code>trans_x</code>, <code>trans_y</code>, <code>trans_z</code>, <code>rot_x</code>, <code>rot_y</code>, <code>rot_z</code>.</li>
                <li><code>motion24</code> — Friston-24 motion model: six motion parameters, their temporal derivatives, squared terms, and squared derivatives.</li>
                <li><code>motion24_wm_csf</code> — Friston-24 motion regressors plus white matter and CSF regressors, including derivatives and squared terms.</li>
                <li><code>motion24_wm_csf_gsr</code> — Friston-24 motion regressors plus white matter, CSF, and global signal regressors. Includes global signal regression and should be used with explicit methodological justification or sensitivity analysis.</li>
                <li><code>acompcor6_motion24</code> — the first six anatomical CompCor components plus Friston-24 motion regressors.</li>
                <li><code>acompcor6_motion24_wm_csf</code> — the first six anatomical CompCor components plus Friston-24 motion regressors, white matter, and CSF regressors.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_denoise_n_compcor">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-denoise-n-compcor <span class="arg">&lt;N&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: 6</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Number of anatomical CompCor components to use when an aCompCor-based denoising strategy is selected. For example, if this value is <code>6</code>, the first six aCompCor components will be used. This parameter only affects strategies containing <code>acompcor</code>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_filter_mode">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-filter-mode <span class="arg">&#123;bandpass|cosine|none&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: bandpass</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the temporal filtering mode used during BOLD denoising.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>bandpass</code> — apply explicit temporal band-pass filtering using <code>--bold-bandpass</code> and exclude fMRIPrep-style cosine regressors.</li>
                <li><code>cosine</code> — use fMRIPrep-style cosine regressors for high-pass drift removal and disable explicit high-pass/low-pass filtering.</li>
                <li><code>none</code> — do not use cosine regressors and do not apply explicit temporal filtering.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_bandpass">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-bandpass <span class="arg">0.01-0.08</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: "0.01-0.08"</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Temporal band-pass frequency range in Hz. Used only when <code>--bold-filter-mode</code> is set to <code>bandpass</code>.</p>
              <p>Example: <code>--bold-bandpass 0.01-0.08</code> means high-pass = 0.01 Hz, low-pass = 0.08 Hz.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_smooth_fwhm">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-smooth-fwhm <span class="arg">0</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: "0"</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Spatial smoothing kernel size in millimeters, specified as full width at half maximum (FWHM). Use <code>0</code> to disable smoothing. Multiple values can be provided to generate multiple smoothed BOLD outputs from the same denoised BOLD image.</p>
              <p><strong>Examples:</strong> <code>--bold-smooth-fwhm 0</code>, <code>--bold-smooth-fwhm 4</code>, <code>--bold-smooth-fwhm 4 6 8</code></p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 id="bold-metrics">Metrics &amp; ROI</h3>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_metrics">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-metrics <span class="arg">reho alff malff zalff falff int</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-type">string</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify one or more BOLD metrics to calculate. Multiple metrics should be provided as a space-separated string.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>reho</code> — regional homogeneity, measuring local synchronization of neighboring voxel time series using Kendall's W.</li>
                <li><code>alff</code> — amplitude of low-frequency fluctuations within the configured frequency band.</li>
                <li><code>malff</code> — mean-normalized ALFF, calculated by dividing voxelwise ALFF by the mean ALFF within the analysis mask.</li>
                <li><code>zalff</code> — Z-score-normalized ALFF, calculated by standardizing voxelwise ALFF values within the analysis mask.</li>
                <li><code>falff</code> — fractional ALFF, calculated as the ratio of low-frequency amplitude to the amplitude across the full available frequency range.</li>
                <li><code>int</code> — intrinsic neural timescale, estimated from the temporal autocorrelation of the BOLD signal.</li>
              </ul>
              <p><strong>Notes:</strong> ReHo is calculated using the time series from which motion frames have been removed. However, the ALFF metrics (and their derivatives) and INT are calculated using the complete sequence, with no motion frames removed.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_alff_bandpass">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-alff-bandpass <span class="arg">0.01-0.08</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: "0.01-0.08"</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specifies the frequency range from which low-frequency amplitudes are extracted during ALFF/fALFF frequency-domain calculations.</p>
              <p>Note that this differs from <code>--bold-bandpass</code>, which is used for time-domain bandpass filtering of BOLD signals. <code>--bold-alff-bandpass</code> is used solely for ALFF/fALFF spectral calculations.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_roi_metrics">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-roi-metrics</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Enable atlas-based ROI summarization of the requested BOLD metrics. For each configured brain atlas, voxelwise metric values are aggregated within each ROI and saved as region-level tabular outputs. When this option is not enabled, only voxelwise metric maps are generated.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_roi_timeseries">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-roi-timeseries</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Extract atlas-based BOLD ROI time series from denoised BOLD images. Requires <a href="#p-cortex_atlas"><code>--cortex-atlas</code></a> and is automatically enabled when <a href="#p-bold_roi_pearson_fc"><code>--bold-roi-pearson-fc</code></a> is enabled.</p>
              <p>The output is saved as an N × T matrix (rows = ROIs, columns = time points). The saved ROI time-series file contains no header, no index, and no ROI label column.</p>
              <p><strong>Notes:</strong> although the time series retains the full timeline, only valid frames that have not been identified as motion artefacts are used to calculate the mean and standard deviation of each ROI for z-score normalisation.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_roi_pearson_fc">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-roi-pearson-fc</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>After excluding any time points flagged as abnormal motion, calculate the Pearson correlation coefficient between two valid ROI time series to construct a static functional connectivity matrix.</p>
              <p>This option automatically enables <code>--bold-roi-timeseries</code>, <code>--bold-denoise</code>, and <code>--bold-confounds</code>.</p>
              <p>The output is an N × N ROI functional connectivity matrix without header or ROI labels.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_roi_fc_censoring">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-roi-fc-censoring</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Controls whether to physically censor (remove) motion frames when computing static functional connectivity. If omitted, the correlation matrix is computed on the full-length time series, where motion frames have been processed according to the specified <code>--bold-scrubbing-strategy</code>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-bold_roi_fc_fisherz">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--bold-roi-fc-fisherz</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Save Fisher-z-transformed Pearson FC values instead of raw Pearson correlation coefficients. Recommended for group-level statistical analysis, edge-wise statistical tests, regression models, or group-average FC calculation. If FC matrices are used directly as graph edge weights for machine learning or GNN models, raw Pearson correlations may be preferable.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="dwi-options">
          <h2>DWI options</h2>

          <h3 id="dwi-basic">DWI basics</h3>

          <div class="param" id="p-dwi_task_type">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--dwi-task-type <span class="arg">task1 task2 task3 ...</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-type">string</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify DWI task or acquisition labels to process when multiple DWI acquisitions are present. Multiple values are passed as space-separated values.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-dwi_sdc_method">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--dwi-sdc-method <span class="arg">&#123;auto|pepolar|fieldmap|synb0|none&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: auto</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the susceptibility distortion correction (SDC) method for DWI.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>auto</code> — automatically select the best available method based on BIDS metadata and participant age.
                  <ul>
                    <li>Adults: <code>pepolar</code> &gt; <code>fieldmap</code> &gt; <code>synb0</code> &gt; <code>none</code>.</li>
                    <li>Infants/Children: <code>pepolar</code> &gt; <code>fieldmap</code> &gt; <code>none</code>.</li>
                  </ul>
                </li>
                <li><code>pepolar</code> — use reverse phase-encoded b0 images for correction (FSL TOPUP).</li>
                <li><code>fieldmap</code> — use GRE-based field maps for distortion correction.</li>
                <li><code>synb0</code> — use Synb0-DISCO to synthesize an undistorted b0 image for correction. Supported for adults only.</li>
                <li><code>none</code> — disable susceptibility distortion correction.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-dwi_volume_res">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--dwi-volume-res <span class="arg">&#123;native|02|03|...&#125;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: 02</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify DWI volumetric output resolution.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>native</code> — keep the native DWI resolution.</li>
                <li><code>01, 02, 03, ...</code> — resample DWI derivatives to the specified isotropic resolution in millimeters.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 id="dwi-tensor">DTI &amp; CSD</h3>

          <div class="param" id="p-dwi_cal_dti">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--dwi-cal-dti</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Compute diffusion tensor imaging metrics.</p>
              <p>Automatically enabled when tensor-based tractography is requested with <a href="#p-fiber_track_algorithm"><code>--fiber-track-algorithm tensor_prob</code></a>, and when FA-weighted connectomes are requested with <a href="#p-dwi_fa_connectome"><code>--dwi-fa-connectome</code></a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-dwi_dti_metrics">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--dwi-dti-metrics <span class="arg">fa md ad rd cl cp cs</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-type">string</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify DTI metrics to compute. This parameter only controls which DTI metrics are generated — DTI metrics are computed only when <a href="#p-dwi_cal_dti"><code>--dwi-cal-dti</code></a> is enabled (or automatically enabled by a dependent option).</p>
              <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                  <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>fa</code></td><td>fractional anisotropy</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>md</code></td><td>mean diffusivity</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>ad</code></td><td>axial diffusivity</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>rd</code></td><td>radial diffusivity</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>cl</code></td><td>linear anisotropy</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>cp</code></td><td>planar anisotropy</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>cs</code></td><td>spherical anisotropy</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-dwi_cal_csd">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--dwi-cal-csd</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Estimate fiber orientation distributions using constrained spherical deconvolution (CSD).</p>
              <p>Automatically enabled when FOD-based tractography algorithms are selected (<code>ifod2</code>, <code>sd_stream</code>). Therefore, if any of <a href="#p-fiber_track_algorithm"><code>--fiber-track-algorithm ifod2</code></a>, <code>--fiber-track-algorithm sd_stream</code>, or <code>--fiber-track-algorithm ifod2 sd_stream</code> is specified, OmniPrep will automatically enable CSD calculation if <code>--dwi-cal-csd</code> has not been explicitly specified.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-dwi_csd_metrics">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--dwi-csd-metrics <span class="arg">wmfod</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-type">string</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify CSD-related outputs to generate when CSD calculation is enabled. Typical outputs may include white matter fiber orientation distributions and related tissue response components, depending on the current implementation.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 id="dwi-track">Tractography</h3>

          <div class="param" id="p-dwi_fiber_track">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--dwi-fiber-track</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Perform whole-brain tractography. Automatically enabled when any of <a href="#p-dwi_create_connectome"><code>--dwi-create-connectome</code></a>, <a href="#p-dwi_fa_connectome"><code>--dwi-fa-connectome</code></a>, or <a href="#p-fiber_track_sift2"><code>--fiber-track-sift2</code></a> is enabled. If tractography is enabled but no tracking algorithm is specified, OmniPrep uses <code>ifod2</code>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-fiber_track_algorithm">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--fiber-track-algorithm <span class="arg">ifod2</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: "ifod2"</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Specify the tractography algorithm or algorithms. Multiple tracking algorithms can be specified simultaneously as space-separated values.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><code>ifod2</code> — probabilistic FOD-based tractography using second-order integration over fiber orientation distributions. Requires CSD.</li>
                <li><code>sd_stream</code> — deterministic FOD-based streamline tractography based on spherical deconvolution. Requires CSD.</li>
                <li><code>tensor_prob</code> — probabilistic tensor-based tractography. Requires DTI.</li>
              </ul>
              <p><strong>Examples:</strong> <code>--fiber-track-algorithm ifod2</code>, <code>ifod2 sd_stream</code>, <code>ifod2 sd_stream tensor_prob</code></p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-fiber_track_select">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--fiber-track-select <span class="arg">&lt;N&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: 10000000</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Number of streamlines to generate or select during tractography.</p>
              <p>Tractography is currently CPU-based and can be one of the most time-consuming steps in OmniPrep.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Routine processing:</strong> 5,000,000 streamlines provides a practical balance between computational cost and tractography quality.</li>
                <li><strong>Higher-quality connectomes:</strong> 10,000,000 streamlines may be used if sufficient computing time is available.</li>
                <li><strong>Testing/debugging:</strong> this value can be reduced, e.g. <code>--fiber-track-select 200000</code>.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-fiber_track_minlength">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--fiber-track-minlength <span class="arg">&lt;N&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: 5</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Minimum streamline length in millimeters.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-fiber_track_maxlength">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--fiber-track-maxlength <span class="arg">&lt;N&gt;</span></span>
              <span class="badge badge-default">default: 250</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Maximum streamline length in millimeters.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-fiber_track_sift2">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--fiber-track-sift2</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Apply SIFT2 to estimate streamline weights after tractography. This option automatically enables <a href="#p-dwi_fiber_track"><code>--dwi-fiber-track</code></a>. Note that OmniPrep currently uses iFOD2-based tractography for SIFT2-weighted derivatives if <code>ifod2</code> is not included in <a href="#p-fiber_track_algorithm"><code>--fiber-track-algorithm</code></a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 id="dwi-connectome">Connectome</h3>

          <div class="param" id="p-dwi_create_connectome">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--dwi-create-connectome</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Construct atlas-based structural connectivity matrices from tractography outputs. Requires a cortical atlas to be specified with <code>--cortex-atlas DK Brainnetome Glasser ...</code>.</p>
              <p>Automatically enables <code>--dwi-fiber-track</code> and <code>--dwi-cal-csd</code>. Note that OmniPrep currently constructs structural connectomes based on iFOD2 tractography if <code>ifod2</code> is not included in <code>--fiber-track-algorithm</code>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-dwi_fa_connectome">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--dwi-fa-connectome</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Compute FA-weighted structural connectivity matrices. Automatically enables <code>--dwi-cal-dti</code>, <code>--dwi-create-connectome</code>, and <code>--dwi-fiber-track</code>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="p-tck2conn_scale_invnodevol">
            <div class="param-head">
              <span class="param-name">--tck2conn-scale-invnodevol</span>
              <span class="badge badge-flag">flag</span>
            </div>
            <div class="param-desc">
              <p>Apply inverse node-volume scaling during structural connectome construction. This option can reduce the influence of ROI size on connectivity estimates by scaling connection weights according to the inverse volume of the connected nodes.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="hpc-env">
          <h2>HPC environment variables (<code>omniprep_singularity.sh</code>)</h2>
          <p class="lead-copy">When running on a SLURM cluster via <code>omniprep_singularity.sh</code>, the wrapper auto-detects GPU and node hardware specs. If you are restricted by scheduler permissions or need to specify a partition or VRAM manually, override the following environment variables:</p>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>OMNIPREP_SINGULARITY_BIN</code></td><td>Path to the Singularity executable</td><td><code>singularity</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>OMNIPREP_NEXTFLOW_BIN</code></td><td>Path to the Nextflow executable</td><td><code>nextflow</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>OMNIPREP_CPU_QUEUE</code></td><td>SLURM partition for CPU tasks</td><td><code>partCU</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>OMNIPREP_GPU_QUEUE</code></td><td>SLURM partition for GPU tasks</td><td><code>partGPU</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>OMNIPREP_SYS_GPU_COUNT</code></td><td>GPU count per compute node</td><td>auto-detected (fallback 4)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>OMNIPREP_SYS_VRAM</code></td><td>Per-GPU VRAM size (MB)</td><td>auto-detected (fallback 40960)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>OMNIPREP_SYS_CPUS</code></td><td>CPU cores per compute node</td><td>auto-detected (fallback 48)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>OMNIPREP_SYS_MEM</code></td><td>Memory per compute node (GB)</td><td>auto-detected (fallback 700)</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="examples">
          <h2>Examples</h2>

          <h3>Run multimodal preprocessing for all subjects</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <div class="cb-head"><span class="cb-label">bash</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
            <pre><code>docker run -it --rm --gpus all \
  -v /path/to/bids:/data:ro -v /path/to/output:/out \
  -v /path/to/license.txt:/license.txt:ro \
  uxhao/omniprep:latest /data /out participant \
  --fs-license-file /license.txt \
  --tasks anat bold dwi \
  [options]</code></pre>
          </div>

          <h3>Run only BOLD preprocessing for selected subjects using existing structural derivatives</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <div class="cb-head"><span class="cb-label">bash</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
            <pre><code>docker run -it --rm --gpus all \
  -v /path/to/bids:/data:ro -v /path/to/output:/out \
  -v /path/to/license.txt:/license.txt:ro \
  uxhao/omniprep:latest /data /out participant \
  --fs-license-file /license.txt \
  --tasks bold \
  --subjects-dir /out/derivatives/omniprep/Recon \
  --participant-label sub-001 sub-002 \
  [options]</code></pre>
          </div>

          <h3>Full BOLD derivatives: denoising, metrics, and functional connectome</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <div class="cb-head"><span class="cb-label">bash</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
            <pre><code>docker run -it --rm --gpus all \
  -v /path/to/bids:/data:ro -v /path/to/output:/out \
  -v /path/to/license.txt:/license.txt:ro \
  uxhao/omniprep:latest /data /out participant \
  --fs-license-file /license.txt \
  --tasks bold \
  --bold-task-type rest \
  --bold-denoise \
  --bold-denoise-strategy motion24_wm_csf \
  --bold-filter-mode bandpass \
  --bold-bandpass 0.01-0.08 \
  --bold-metrics reho alff falff \
  --cortex-atlas DK Brainnetome \
  --bold-roi-pearson-fc \
  --bold-roi-fc-fisherz</code></pre>
          </div>

          <h3>DWI: CSD tractography and a structural connectome</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <div class="cb-head"><span class="cb-label">bash</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
            <pre><code>docker run -it --rm --gpus all \
  -v /path/to/bids:/data:ro -v /path/to/output:/out \
  -v /path/to/license.txt:/license.txt:ro \
  uxhao/omniprep:latest /data /out participant \
  --fs-license-file /license.txt \
  --tasks dwi \
  --dwi-sdc-method auto \
  --fiber-track-algorithm ifod2 \
  --fiber-track-select 10000000 \
  --cortex-atlas DK Brainnetome \
  --dwi-create-connectome \
  --tck2conn-scale-invnodevol</code></pre>
          </div>
        </section>

